title: Round 3 — BrowserVideoFrameProvider + srcResolver close the disk-loaded-media gap
summary: |-
  Round 2 fixes verified at runtime by owner: canvas-size dropdown visible, frame ruler horizontal, canvas letterbox-fits. Canvas still showed black where the video should play — diagnosis: renderFrame's videoFrameProvider option was wired through the renderer but NO preview-mode implementation existed anywhere in the codebase, and canvas-panel was calling renderFrame with only ImageCache (no provider). Every VideoVisual layer silently skipped via the if(videoFrameProvider) guard. Wrote BrowserVideoFrameProvider (HTMLVideoElement-backed, seek-debounced at 16ms epsilon, returns null during in-flight seeks, fires onReady on loadeddata/seeked so canvas-panel re-paints). Also added StudioOptions.srcResolver to map doc-stored relative srcs (media/IMG_7346.MOV) → browser-fetchable URLs (/api/file?path=…) — closing a latent gap where disk-loaded docs with image layers ALSO couldn't fetch bytes (drag-drop image-drop was masking it via data-URLs). Workspace-app + inline-app both supply the resolver rooted at the loaded doc's directory. Caption-stacking concern from owner screenshot investigated separately via probe script: resolveFrame is correct — at frame 86 only cap-1 should be visible, at frame 89 cap-1 fading out + cap-2 fading in (cross-fade). Owner likely caught a cross-fade moment in the original screenshot; needs re-verification post-video-render to confirm captions display one at a time.</summary>
  <parameter name="symbols_touched">["#browser-video-frame-provider", "#canvas-panel", "#atelier-studio", "#workspace-app", "#inline-app"]
